                    {
                        "sense_id": "38a7593b-4516-372e-a910-754d0e97cba4",
                        "entry_id": "e16f7a56-0267-304a-a924-5f4880120503",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To move with, or make, a crashing or rustling sound."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Scotland"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "89bd6c62-1212-41f7-8bf4-b50bfb732feb",
                                "sense_id": "38a7593b-4516-372e-a910-754d0e97cba4",
                                "text": "[…] and once snow slurred upon the root and thudded reeshling to the ground."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1ac24618-85a8-4162-916d-30d95fda7731",
                                "sense_id": "38a7593b-4516-372e-a910-754d0e97cba4",
                                "text": "... their pows, An' their shin-banes reeshle i' their hose, An' sigh an grane, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a38248aa-c944-4fc0-b8f5-ddad89381bf6",
                                "sense_id": "38a7593b-4516-372e-a910-754d0e97cba4",
                                "text": "He could hear them reeshling up the river bank. And their feet clanking along the footpath. They were running away […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "615db0f8-90be-43fb-926a-d6cf3fbbb1a2",
                                "sense_id": "38a7593b-4516-372e-a910-754d0e97cba4",
                                "text": "The ever-shifting whoosh of water and the reeshling of leaves came from her lips as they moved."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4b2f8489-2c10-4134-8cdb-af8bed3a8c87",
                                "sense_id": "38a7593b-4516-372e-a910-754d0e97cba4",
                                "text": "At this, the whooshing, brattling, reeshling sound becomes laughter, rattling the windowpanes and bursting past Callum on its way out the door, and as he staggers backwards, he thinks he hears it whistling off, down the lane, off up the green hill past the monument[…]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
